IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cma-types`
IMPORT `cma-definitions`
IMPORT `cma-offences`

-- Computer Misuse Act 1993 — GOAL 3: THE MOST AN OFFENCE CAN COST
-- (ss 3-11; caning in ss 8A(5), 8B(5A)-(5B); s 12).
--
--   "If convicted, what is the maximum fine, term of imprisonment and number
--    of strokes?"
--
-- Every limb reads "a fine not exceeding $X or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding Y years or ... both"; the record holds each ceiling. Strokes are
-- 0 unless the section provides caning.
-- Source: ../source/CMA1993.txt lines 159-530.

§ `Goal 3 — punishment`

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CMA punishment`
`punishment of` f y c MEANS `CMA punishment` WITH `fine` IS f, `imprisonment in years` IS y, `caning strokes` IS c

§§ `The section's own ceilings`

-- s 3(1): "(a) ... $5,000 ... 2 years ...; and (b) in the case of a second or
-- subsequent conviction, ... $10,000 ... 3 years"; s 3(2): "If any damage is
-- caused as a result of an offence under this section ... $50,000 ... 7 years".
-- s 4(3): "$50,000 ... 10 years".
-- ss 5(1)-(2), 6(1)-(2), 7(1)-(2): "$10,000 ... 3 years"; second or
-- subsequent "$20,000 ... 5 years"; damage "$50,000 ... 7 years".
-- s 8(2), 8B(5), 9(5), 10(3): "$10,000 ... 3 years"; second or subsequent
-- "$20,000 ... 5 years".
-- s 8A(1): "$10,000 ... 3 years", with no higher limb for a repeat conviction.
@ref ss 3(1)-(2); 4(3); 5(1)-(2); 6(1)-(2); 7(1)-(2); 8(2); 8A(1); 8B(5); 9(5); 10(3)
GIVEN o IS AN `Alleged offence`, repeat IS A BOOLEAN, damaged IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `CMA punishment`
`the section's punishment for` o `, repeat:` repeat `, damage caused:` damaged MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` a b c d                              THEN `with damage` 5000  2 10000 3
    WHEN `s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` a b c                                 THEN `punishment of` 50000 10 0
    WHEN `s 5 unauthorised modification of computer material` a b c                         THEN `with damage` 10000 3 20000 5
    WHEN `s 6 unauthorised use or interception of computer service` a b c d                 THEN `with damage` 10000 3 20000 5
    WHEN `s 7 unauthorised obstruction of use of computer` a b c                            THEN `with damage` 10000 3 20000 5
    WHEN `s 8 unauthorised disclosure of access code` a b c d                               THEN `repeat or not` 10000 3 20000 5
    WHEN `s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` a b c d e f THEN `punishment of` 10000 3 0
    WHEN `s 8B dealing in another person's credential` a f s                                THEN `repeat or not` 10000 3 20000 5
    WHEN `s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` a b f         THEN `repeat or not` 10000 3 20000 5
    WHEN `s 10 obtaining items for use in certain offences` a b c d                         THEN `repeat or not` 10000 3 20000 5
    WHERE
        `repeat or not` f1 y1 f2 y2 MEANS
            IF repeat THEN `punishment of` f2 y2 0 ELSE `punishment of` f1 y1 0
        -- "If any damage is caused ... a person convicted of the offence
        -- shall be liable to ..." — in place of (1), whether or not a repeat.
        `with damage` f1 y1 f2 y2 MEANS
            IF damaged THEN `punishment of` 50000 7 0 ELSE `repeat or not` f1 y1 f2 y2

§§ `Protected computers (s 11)`

-- s 11(1): "Where access to any protected computer is obtained in the course
-- of the commission of an offence under section 3, 5, 6 or 7, a person
-- convicted of the offence shall, in lieu of the punishment prescribed in those
-- sections, be liable to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 20 years or to both."
-- s 11(2): "protected" if the offender "knew, or ought reasonably to have
-- known" the computer, program or data is used for (a)-(d).
-- s 11(3): knowledge "is presumed, until the contrary is proved" where a
-- warning "that unauthorised access ... attracts an enhanced penalty under this
-- section" was exhibited.
@ref s 11(2)-(3)
GIVEN p IS A `Protected computer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a protected computer` p IF
        NOT p's `use` EQUALS `none of the s 11(2) uses`
    AND (   p's `the accused knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the use`
         OR (    p's `a warning of the enhanced penalty was exhibited to the accused`
             AND NOT p's `the contrary of the presumed knowledge is proved`))

@ref s 11(1)
GIVEN o IS AN `Alleged offence`, p IS A `Protected computer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11 enhances the punishment for` o `, protected computer:` p IF
        `an offence under s 3, 5, 6 or 7` o
    AND p's `access to the computer was obtained in the course of the offence`
    AND `a protected computer` p

GIVEN o IS AN `Alleged offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under s 3, 5, 6 or 7` o IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` a b c d               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 5 unauthorised modification of computer material` a b c          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 6 unauthorised use or interception of computer service` a b c d  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 7 unauthorised obstruction of use of computer` a b c             THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Caning (ss 8A(5), 8B(5A)-(5B))`

-- s 8A(5): an individual convicted "shall, in addition ..., be liable to caning
-- of not more than 12 strokes — (a) if the individual knew that the purpose
-- ... was ... any scam offence; or (b) if — (i) it is proved ... that the
-- password, access code, or means of securing access, was used to commit, or
-- to facilitate the commission of, a scam offence; and (ii) the individual is
-- not able to prove ... that he or she had, at any time, taken reasonable
-- steps to ensure that [it] would not be used" for one.
-- s 8B(5A): convicted under (1)(a), 12 strokes if the credential was obtained
-- or retained "(a) for use in committing ... any scam offence; or (b) for the
-- supply ... [of] the credential to be used in committing ... any scam
-- offence". s 8B(5B): convicted under (1)(b), as s 8A(5).
@ref ss 8A(5)-(7); 8B(5A)-(5D)
GIVEN o IS AN `Alleged offence`, individual IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the caning strokes for` o `, an individual:` individual MEANS
    IF NOT individual THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER o
         WHEN `s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` a b c d e scam THEN
             IF `knowing or unexcused scam use` scam THEN 12 ELSE 0
         WHEN `s 8B dealing in another person's credential` a facts scam THEN
             CONSIDER facts's `dealing`
             WHEN `(a) obtains or retains` THEN
                 IF scam's `obtained or retained it for a scam offence, or for supply for one` THEN 12 ELSE 0
             WHEN `(b) supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available` THEN
                 IF `knowing or unexcused scam use` scam THEN 12 ELSE 0
         OTHERWISE 0

@ref ss 8A(5)(a)-(b); 8B(5B)(a)-(b)
GIVEN s IS A `Scam facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `knowing or unexcused scam use` s IF
        s's `knew the purpose or use was a scam offence`
    OR  (    s's `proved to the court it was used for a scam offence`
         AND NOT s's `the accused proved reasonable steps against its use for a scam offence`)

§§ `The maximum punishment`

-- s 12(1): abetment, attempt and preparatory acts carry "the punishment
-- provided for the offence", so participation does not change the answer.
@ref ss 3-12
GIVEN o IS AN `Alleged offence`, repeat IS A BOOLEAN, damaged IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A `Protected computer facts`, individual IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `CMA punishment`
`the maximum punishment for` o `, repeat:` repeat `, damage caused:` damaged `, protected computer:` p `, an individual:` individual MEANS
    IF   `s 11 enhances the punishment for` o `, protected computer:` p
    THEN `punishment of` 100000 20 0
    ELSE `punishment of` (`base`'s `fine`) (`base`'s `imprisonment in years`) (`the caning strokes for` o `, an individual:` individual)
    WHERE
        `base` MEANS `the section's punishment for` o `, repeat:` repeat `, damage caused:` damaged
